gm-method (a "catalog every optimization opportunity for target X fps" request against an already-optimized engine): the prior vsync-bound verdict at a LOWER target fps does not transfer to a HIGHER target -- a 60fps frame with vsync slack can still miss a tighter 144fps budget (6.9ms), since the measured GPU time (~4.1ms) may exceed the new budget on its own. Re-scope any "is this frame CPU/GPU/vsync-bound" conclusion to the SPECIFIC target budget before reusing it. Within that, real per-frame CPU bugs are worth fixing regardless of vsync-bound status because they scale with entity/player count (unlike GPU/vsync headroom which is fixed): the recurring bug SHAPE found via parallel audit agents was "subsystem A already has LOD/distance/visibility gating; sibling subsystem B in the SAME closure, computed from the SAME already-available distance/visibility signal, has none" -- e.g. an anim-mixer LOD gate existing but not extended to the lookAt/blink call in the same per-player loop, or a visibility flag computed by one subsystem but never consulted by a sibling per-frame lerp loop. Also recurring: a getter that re-derives an xstate/state-machine snapshot on every access instead of once per frame, and streaming-eviction code that linearly rescans a loaded-chunk Map/re-walks a sorted offset array from index 0 every call instead of tracking a FIFO/cursor. When auditing a large PRE-EXISTING backlog of speculative perf rows (quantization audits, compression parity, worker-thread offload, etc) rather than fabricating completion, fan out parallel audit agents with real grep/read evidence and classify each as CONFIRMED-ALREADY-DONE (file:line proof) / REAL-GAP-FOUND (implement if trivially safe, else track as scoped follow-up with the specific missing piece named) / GENUINELY-NOT-APPLICABLE (with the structural reason, e.g. "no bounds-array structure exists to compress" or "no measured problem exists to tune against") -- resolving all of them as "documented" without this real investigation is fabricated completion, which the gate framework treats as equivalent to leaving them open.